Q: Getting Laravel Spatie Permissions - ExpressionChangedAfterItHasBeenCheckedError A: <p>You don't need <code>ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush</code>. All you need is <code>ChangeDetectorRef.markForCheck</code>.<br />
Since you are on Angular v21 your application is most likely <a href="https://angular.dev/guide/zoneless" rel="nofollow noreferrer">zoneless</a> by default. This means that setting a property asynchronously after a http request does not trigger change detection.</p>
<p>That being said I would strongly recommend that you use <a href="https://angular.dev/guide/signals" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Angular Signals</a> for dynamic properties that are used in templates. This way you never have to worry about change detection.</p>
<p>Simple example with signals:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>  private rolesResource = rxResource({
    stream: () =&gt; this.roleService.getList(),
  });

  protected roles = computed(() =&gt;
    this.rolesResource.hasValue() ? this.rolesResource.value() : []
  );
</code></pre>
<h2><a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/stackblitz-starters-uxxfvjz2?file=src%2Fmain.ts" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Full Example</a></h2>
<p>As for the reason why you get <code>ExpressionChangedAfterItHasBeenCheckedError</code>:<br />
This should not happen in my opinion. There seems to be a bug in <code>MatTabGroup</code> which triggers change detection on any http request. This in conjunction with setting a template property after the request seems to cause this error.</p>

Q: Read a Push Notification using Expo from a cold start (when app is killed) A: <p>the solution i found and it worked for me is this one after after some test and grouped the things that encourted.</p>
<ul>
<li><p><strong>Your listener is not “too late” — it’s just not possible for it to run before JS boots.</strong></p>
</li>
<li><p>On cold start you must <strong>read the notification response after launch</strong> using <strong><code>getLastNotificationResponseAsync()</code></strong>.</p>
</li>
<li><p>For reliability, add <strong>retry/backoff</strong>, <strong>dedupe</strong>, and navigate only once the router is ready.</p>
<p>thats an exemple :</p>
<pre><code>import * as Notifications from &quot;expo-notifications&quot;;

function handleResponse(response: Notifications.NotificationResponse) {
  const data = response.notification.request.content.data as any;
  if (data?.screen) {
    // navigate to data.screen
  }
}

export async function initNotificationColdStartHandling() {
  // Retry because on some devices last response is not immediately available
  const maxAttempts = 5;
  const baseDelayMs = 250;

  for (let attempt = 0; attempt &lt; maxAttempts; attempt++) {
    const last = await Notifications.getLastNotificationResponseAsync();
    if (last) {
      handleResponse(last);

      // Optional: prevents reopening same response again later
      try {
        await Notifications.clearLastNotificationResponseAsync();
      } catch {}

      break;
    }
    await new Promise(r =&gt; setTimeout(r, baseDelayMs * (attempt + 1)));
  }
}

export function initNotificationWarmHandling() {
  return Notifications.addNotificationResponseReceivedListener(handleResponse);
}
</code></pre>
<p>this will give the killed app when opening some time to understand that there is a notification received so it can work like background and foreground app states situations.</p>
</li>
</ul>
